{"name":"Wall Street","hex":"#656d73","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Wall Street","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["American financial institutions or financial markets as a whole;  big-business interests.","The street that traditionally has been a principal locus for those entities and whose name is metonymically extended to refer to them."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Wall_Street"}],"entries":[{"title":"Wall Street","blocks":[{"text":"Wall Street is a street in the Financial District of Lower Manhattan in New York City. It runs eight city blocks between Broadway in the west and South Street and the East River in the east with a length of just under 2,000 feet. The term \"Wall Street\" has become a metonym for New York Stock Exchange (NYSE), the financial markets of the United States, American financial services industry, New York–based financial interests, or the Financial District. Anchored by Wall Street, New York has been described as the world's principal fintech and financial center."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Wall_Street_%2855314253740%29.jpg/330px-Wall_Street_%2855314253740%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wall_Street"},{"title":"Wall Street (1987 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Wall Street is a 1987 American crime drama film directed and co-written by Oliver Stone, which stars Michael Douglas, Charlie Sheen, Daryl Hannah, and Martin Sheen. The film tells the story of Bud Fox, a young stockbroker who becomes involved with Gordon Gekko (Douglas), a wealthy, unscrupulous corporate raider."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/bc/Wall_Street_film.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wall_Street_(1987_film)"},{"title":"Wall","blocks":[{"text":"A wall is a structure and a surface that defines an area; carries a load; provides security, shelter, or soundproofing; or serves a decorative purpose. There are various types of walls, including border barriers between countries, brick walls, defensive walls in fortifications, and retaining walls that hold back dirt, stone, water, or noise. Walls can also be found in buildings, where they support roofs, floors, and ceilings, enclose spaces, and provide shelter and security."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Noel_2005_P%C3%A9kin_031_muraille_de_chine_Mutianyu.jpg/330px-Noel_2005_P%C3%A9kin_031_muraille_de_chine_Mutianyu.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wall"},{"title":"Street","blocks":[{"text":"A street is a public thoroughfare in a city, town or village, typically lined with buildings on one or both sides. Streets often include pavements (sidewalks), pedestrian crossings, and sometimes amenities like streetlights or benches. A street can be as simple as a level patch of dirt, but is more often paved with a hard, durable surface such as tarmac, concrete, cobblestone or brick. It can be designed for both social activity and movement."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Typical_Street_In_The_Royal_Borough_Of_Kensington_And_Chelsea_In_London.jpg/330px-Typical_Street_In_The_Royal_Borough_Of_Kensington_And_Chelsea_In_London.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Street"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/Wall_Street_Sign_%281-9%29.jpg/500px-Wall_Street_Sign_%281-9%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/Wall_Street_Sign_%281-9%29.jpg/1280px-Wall_Street_Sign_%281-9%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/Wall_Street_Sign_%281-9%29.jpg/500px-Wall_Street_Sign_%281-9%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Street sign","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWall_Street_Sign_(1-9).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Stad_Amsterdam_in_Nieuw_Nederland_%28City_Amsterdam_in_New_Netherland%29_Castello_Plan_1660.jpg/500px-Stad_Amsterdam_in_Nieuw_Nederland_%28City_Amsterdam_in_New_Netherland%29_Castello_Plan_1660.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Stad_Amsterdam_in_Nieuw_Nederland_%28City_Amsterdam_in_New_Netherland%29_Castello_Plan_1660.jpg/1280px-Stad_Amsterdam_in_Nieuw_Nederland_%28City_Amsterdam_in_New_Netherland%29_Castello_Plan_1660.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Stad_Amsterdam_in_Nieuw_Nederland_%28City_Amsterdam_in_New_Netherland%29_Castello_Plan_1660.jpg/500px-Stad_Amsterdam_in_Nieuw_Nederland_%28City_Amsterdam_in_New_Netherland%29_Castello_Plan_1660.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The original city map, called the Castello Plan, from 1660, showing the wall on the right side","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AStad_Amsterdam_in_Nieuw_Nederland_(City_Amsterdam_in_New_Netherland)_Castello_Plan_1660.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Block-House_and_City_Gate_%28foot_of_present_Wall_Street%29_1674_New_Amsterdam.jpg/500px-Block-House_and_City_Gate_%28foot_of_present_Wall_Street%29_1674_New_Amsterdam.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Block-House_and_City_Gate_%28foot_of_present_Wall_Street%29_1674_New_Amsterdam.jpg/1280px-Block-House_